# Example .gitignore for a real notes vault synced with Git.
# Goal:
# - keep notes and shareable vault configuration under version control
# - ignore local session state, OS noise, and the bundled portable Git
# - stay compatible with automatic backups via obsidian-git

# Repository metadata
.git/

# Portable Git bundled with this template.
# Ignore it in a real notes repo unless you explicitly want to version binaries.
.obsidian/git_portable/

# Local Obsidian session state regenerated on each machine.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Trash and OS noise
.trash/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Optional: ignore local plugin data that tends to be machine-specific.
# Leave these commented unless you confirm they add noise in your setup.
# .obsidian/plugins/obsidian-git/data.json
# .obsidian/plugins/notebook-navigator/data.json

# Optional: ignore generated exports or heavy attachments if your vault uses them.
# Uncomment only if you do not want them in the notes backup repo.
# Excalidraw/**/*.png
# Excalidraw/**/*.svg
# Attachments/
